-# Verification report: walmart-azure-headless 1.6.1
+# Verification report: walmart-azure-headless 1.6.2
+
+## Release 1.6.2
+
+Release 1.6.2 corrects two defects that this delivery's live runs of 2026-11-03 found with release 1.6.1. Offline
+tests show each defect and its correction: each new test of a change fails on 1.6.1 and passes on 1.6.2, and the
+tests that show what did not change pass on both. Live results are not recorded here: the delivery's review
+documents give each live stage, the frozen build it ran on and its result.
+
+| Change | Until 1.6.1 | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| A listing whose total moved while it was read, and whose served results fall short of its smallest reported total by more than the total moved (however they are counted: placed identities or tiles), ends at the site's result window (`RESULT_WINDOW`, "accessible pages exhausted; coverage incomplete", with the range of totals reported) and is partitioned through its child categories like any listing past its window. It is never `DONE`: its own total moved, so nothing can reconcile it | The listing ended "not reconciled" without a window end, and was not partitioned. Live on 2026-11-03: Laundry reported 615, 613, 614 and 611 results while it was read, the site served 393, and page 11 of the 16 it linked was empty; Shampoo reported 608 and 607, the site served 399, and page 12 was empty | `collection/walmart.py` (`close_listing`, `_short_whatever_the_count`); `tests/unit/test_listing_reconciliation.py::test_a_moving_total_far_above_what_the_site_served_is_a_result_window_never_done` and `tests/integration/test_coverage_and_assortment.py::test_a_moving_total_does_not_hide_a_window_end_and_the_listing_is_read_through_its_children` (both fail on 1.6.1); `tests/unit/test_listing_reconciliation.py::test_a_shortfall_no_larger_than_the_totals_moved_stays_unreconciled_not_a_window` (unchanged; passes on both) |
+| A listing link that serves a category page (a page of links without a result grid: its data is the page `/cp/[...categoryParams]`) is recorded `INCOMPLETE` with the end `CATEGORY_PAGE`, the category page it served and the listings that page links. The run goes on and the store is not held. It is never an empty listing, and no product is taken from that page | The run stopped (`ABNORMAL_RESULT`, exit 6, not resumable) and the store was held until `release-hold`, as for a page of unknown shape. Live on 2026-11-03: the Food navigation's link "Fresh Flowers" (`/browse/food/flowers/976759_1089004_2424807`) served the category page "Flower Shop" (`/cp/flower-shop/5098771`), and the census stopped after 29 listing pages | `sites/walmart/page_data.py` (`category_page`), `collection/walmart.py` (`_page`); `tests/unit/test_walmart.py::test_a_category_page_is_told_from_its_own_data_and_no_other_page_is_one` and `tests/integration/test_coverage_and_assortment.py::test_a_listing_link_that_serves_a_category_page_is_recorded_unread_and_the_run_goes_on` (both fail on 1.6.1); `tests/integration/test_coverage_and_assortment.py::test_any_other_page_without_a_result_grid_still_stops_the_run` (a page of unknown shape, or a category page after a listing's first result page: still `ABNORMAL_RESULT`; passes on both) |
+
+The listings such a category page links are named, not read: whether they belong to the row's scope is the client's
+decision. The "Flower Shop" page links Food listings (Roses, Tulips, Mixed bouquets and others) and listings under
+Home and Patio & Garden (artificial flowers, indoor plants, orchids). Any other page without a result grid still
+stops the run and holds the store.
 
